  bootwright
      Coordinate declarative day-0 platform bootstrap

  Usage
    bootwright [flags]

  Start
  COMMAND      PURPOSE
  context      Manage context
  controller   Manage controller
  validate     Validate a complete desired-state input universe
  preflight    Manage preflight

  Lifecycle
  COMMAND   PURPOSE
  plan      Preview the next complete lifecycle operation
  apply     Apply the complete selected lifecycle unit
  destroy   Destroy the complete selected lifecycle unit
  status    Show context readiness and lifecycle state
  diff      Compare desired state with what this context realized

  Resources
  COMMAND   PURPOSE
  machine   Manage machine
  cluster   Manage cluster
  media     Manage media
  secret    Manage secret
  add-ons   Manage add-ons
  render    Render external-tool artifacts

  Tools
  COMMAND      PURPOSE
  version      Show executable and dependency build identities
  completion   Manage completion
  help         Show help for an exact command path

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright help context init
    bootwright version
    bootwright validate --file ./input
